@startuml
title Relational Access V1 - L4 Transaction and Shard Boundary
autonumber

participant "Idempotency Executor" as Exec
participant "Transaction Coordinator" as Tx
participant "Business Mapper" as Biz
participant "SpringMyBatisAccess" as Access
participant "Idempotency Mapper" as Idem
database "Same physical DB" as DB

Exec -> Tx : REQUIRED(routeKey)
Tx -> DB : begin / join local transaction
Tx -> Biz : business write
Biz -> DB : SQL using shardKey
Tx -> Access : executeInCurrentTransaction(markSuccess)
Access -> Access : require bound DataSource
note right of Access
Constructor validates DataSource / Environment pairing.
execute() also checks binding when an actual transaction exists.
Listener RuntimeException cannot change the Mapper outcome.
end note
Access -> Idem : SUCCESS CAS(owner, version)
Idem -> DB : same transaction resource

alt CAS updated
  Tx -> DB : commit business + SUCCESS
  Tx --> Exec : EXECUTED
else stale owner / provider error
  Tx -> DB : rollback all local writes
  Tx --> Exec : completion rejected
end

note over Biz,Idem
Same MyBatis framework is not sufficient.
Both mappers must resolve to the same local transaction resource.
Cross-shard atomicity needs middleware distributed transactions or a different design.
end note
@enduml
